ber to November is the driest pair on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, with a normal of 4.88 inches, and it came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years since 1951. In 2025 the middle ran 29% of normal in September to October. So far in 2026 it ran 32% of normal in March to April and 222% of normal in May to June. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, as low as 52% of normal.</p>"}
